# Copy this to deploy/site.env (gitignored -- never commit the copy) and
# fill in the passphrase the published site sits behind.
#
# This is a third password, and all three are separate:
#   SITE_PASSWORD        reading the published site  (this file)
#   DASHBOARD_PASSWORD   the admin tool at /admin    (deploy/dashboard.env)
#   the deploy key       pushing to GitHub           (no password at all)
#
# It lives in a file rather than in a shell variable because a shell
# variable lasts as long as the shell, and two things read this: the
# public site (public.py) at every service start, and the archive build
# at every build -- including the one a nightly timer runs, where there
# is no shell and nobody to remember.
#
# It is also what session cookies are signed with, so changing this and
# restarting corpusvic-public ends every session that exists. That is the
# thing to do if it ever leaks.
#
# Leaving the file absent does not quietly open anything. The site
# refuses to start without it and asks for --open; the archive build
# refuses to replace a gated build and asks for --no-password. Pages
# served once in the clear stay served, so both want the choice made
# rather than arrived at.
SITE_PASSWORD=
